{{/* stack: layout of pre-rendered children, with no surface of its own. Inline forms
     a wrapping row of acts a control's 32px tall, so a control's edges are
     the row's (a subsection act's 28px stands 2px in, the row reading its
     acts by their verso-act mark), its wrapped rows 40px apart; Divided draws hairlines; Compact tightens the default vertical rhythm. A
     plain stack names itself (verso-stack): as the page's root it takes the
     page rhythm from input.css — its blocks 2.5rem apart. A flush stack adds
     no rhythm and says it holds rows (data-verso-rows), so a section gives
     back its first and last rows' air as if they stood in it directly. */}}
<div{{if and .Flush (not .Inline)}} data-verso-rows{{end}} class="{{if eq .Width "compact"}}max-w-md {{end}}{{if .Inline}}flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 has-[.verso-act]:gap-y-3 has-[.verso-act]:py-0.5{{else if .Flush}}{{else if .Divided}}divide-y divide-rule{{else if .Compact}}space-y-3{{else if .Loose}}verso-stack space-y-10{{else}}verso-stack space-y-6{{end}}">{{range .Children}}{{.}}{{end}}</div>
